note leak fixture (flags rule, README.txt; contract spec/omegese-om2.md section 8 lines 234-236): a
note comparison of a loaded byte is materialized with CSET into b, then a comparison of the public n
note sets the flags again. The second compare replaces the flags' taint (last flag-setting op), so the
note branch on c is len, while the branch on b (CSET of data flags) is data MANUAL under E12.
note Expected: TRACE-EQUIV-STATIC NOT_RUN with exactly one data branch.
fn f a view uchar 16 n ulong to ulong
b = lt ulong get a 0 5
